# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
import tests/cadkernel/brep_intersect/helpers.dl

set one to intersect sphere at [0.0,0.0,2.0] radius 5.0
set other to intersect cylinder at [0.0,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0] radius 3.0
set meeting to the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9
check intersect curves meeting on one and other
check intersect ((the length of meeting's curves) = 2)
intersect near ((the item at 0 in meeting's curves)'s circle's plane's origin's z) to -2.0
intersect near ((the item at 1 in meeting's curves)'s circle's plane's origin's z) to 6.0
set other to intersect cylinder at [0.0,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,-1.0] radius 3.0
set reversed to the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9
check intersect curves reversed on one and other
intersect near ((the item at 0 in reversed's curves)'s circle's plane's origin's z) to 6.0
intersect near ((the item at 1 in reversed's curves)'s circle's plane's origin's z) to -2.0
set other to intersect cylinder at [0.0,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0] radius 5.0
set meeting to the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9
check intersect curves meeting on one and other
check intersect ((the length of meeting's curves) = 1)
intersect near ((the item at 0 in meeting's curves)'s circle's plane's origin's z) to 2.0
set other to intersect cylinder at [0.0,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0] radius 6.0
check intersect ((the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9) = (no cad surface meeting))
set other to intersect cylinder at [0.01,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0] radius 3.0
check intersect ((the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9) = (an unknown cad surface meeting))
set other to intersect cylinder at [0.0,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0] radius 0.0
check intersect ((the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9) = (an unknown cad surface meeting))
print "coaxial_sphere_cylinder_preserves_latitude_order_and_refusals" as a line

set one to intersect cone
set other to intersect cylinder at [0.0,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0] radius 3.0
set meeting to the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9
check intersect curves meeting on one and other
check intersect ((the length of meeting's curves) = 2)
intersect near ((the item at 0 in meeting's curves)'s circle's plane's origin's z) to 7.0
intersect near ((the item at 1 in meeting's curves)'s circle's plane's origin's z) to 13.0
check intersect (meeting = (the cad meeting of other and one within 1e-9))
set other to intersect cylinder at [0.0,0.0,4.0] normal [0.0,0.0,-1.0] radius 3.0
set meeting to the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9
check intersect curves meeting on one and other
check intersect ((the length of meeting's curves) = 2)
set other to intersect cylinder at [0.0,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0] radius 0.0
check intersect ((the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9) = (no cad surface meeting))
print "cone_cylinder_keeps_both_nappes_and_skips_apex_only_roots" as a line

set otherFrame to the cad xy plane
set otherFrame's origin to intersect point [0.0,0.0,2.0]
set other to the cad surface of (a cad cone with base otherFrame, radius 3.0 and half angle 0.19739555984988078)
set meeting to the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9
check intersect curves meeting on one and other
check intersect ((the length of meeting's curves) = 2)
check intersect ((the cad meeting of one and one within 1e-9) = (a coincident cad surface meeting))
set one to the cad surface of (a cad cone with base (the cad xy plane), radius 5.0 and half angle 0.0)
set other to the cad surface of (a cad cone with base (the cad xy plane), radius 3.0 and half angle 0.0)
check intersect ((the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9) = (no cad surface meeting))
print "coaxial_cones_solve_both_signs_and_parallel_denominators" as a line

set one to intersect cone
set other to intersect plane at [0.0,0.0,15.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0]
set meeting to the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9
check intersect curves meeting on one and other
intersect near ((the item at 0 in meeting's curves)'s circle's radius) to 5.0
set one to intersect cylinder at [0.0,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0] radius 5.0
set other to intersect cylinder at [10.0,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0] radius 5.0
set meeting to the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9
check intersect curves meeting on one and other
check intersect ((the length of meeting's curves) = 1)
intersect near ((the item at 0 in meeting's curves)'s line's origin's x) to 5.0
print "mirrored_cone_and_tangent_cylinders_remain_exact" as a line

set badFrame to a cad plane with origin (the cad zero vector3), x axis (the cad zero vector3) and y axis (the cad y axis)
set one to the cad surface of badFrame
set other to the cad surface of (the cad xy plane)
check intersect ((the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9) = (an unknown cad surface meeting))
set one to the cad surface of (a cad sphere with frame badFrame and radius 5.0)
set other to intersect cylinder at [0.0,0.0,0.0] normal [0.0,0.0,1.0] radius 3.0
check intersect ((the cad meeting of one and other within 1e-9) = (an unknown cad surface meeting))
print "degenerate_required_frames_return_unknown" as a line
